exports[`the rules pages in English setup keeps its text and links 1`] = `
{
  "links": [
    "/wiki/rules/turn Turn Structure",
  ],
  "text": [
    "Setup",
    "What happens before the first turn.",
    "Every seat is dealt 5 Generals. Each set includes at least two Generals of the same Force.",
    "Each player chooses two of their Generals: a Main General and a Deputy General. Both start face down.",
    "HP is shared: half the sum of the two Generals' HP, rounded down. Damage and healing apply to this one pool.",
    "The draw pile is shuffled and every seat draws 4 cards.",
    "Revealing Generals",
    "At the start of your own turn, before anything else happens, a window lists your hidden Generals and you may reveal any of them, or none.",
    "In your own Play Phase a General is revealed only by using something of it that you can use, such as an active skill or a conversion, which reveals it first. You cannot reveal one for no reason.",
    "In any phase of any turn, when something happens that a hidden skill answers, such as taking damage or losing equipment, you are asked whether to reveal its General to use the skill. Losing HP never reveals a General by itself.",
    "When you reveal your second General and the two Generals' HP added together was odd (so your HP was rounded down), you draw 1 card.",
    "Optional, with 5 or more seats: the first seat to reveal a General draws 2 cards. This is a checkbox in Game Setup.",
    "When a seat dies, both its Generals are revealed. No reveal bonus is drawn for it.",
    "Killing a seat",
    "When a seat is eliminated, the seat whose damage killed it is rewarded or penalized.",
    "Different Force: the killer draws one card for each living seat of the dead seat's Force, counting the dead seat itself.",
    "Same Force: the killer discards its entire hand.",
    "A killer who has not revealed either General always counts as a different Force, even if it secretly shares the dead seat's Force.",
    "Qun counts as one Force like the others.",
    "Nothing happens if the death had no source, the seat killed itself, or the killer is out as well.",
    "Next: Turn Structure.",
  ],
}
`;

